IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vca-core`

-- Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976 (Tas) -- from the seat of THE APPLICANT: a primary, secondary or related victim
-- of an offence, or a person who paid (or will pay) a primary victim's funeral expenses. "Can I apply, and as which
-- kind of victim? Which heads of compensation can I claim? Is my claim excluded, and does it belong to MAIB or
-- workers compensation instead? What is the most I can be awarded? What would I be paid? By when must I apply, and
-- by when must it be decided? What must my application contain?" Every question is phrased as that person asks it,
-- on facts that person could state. The rules are in vca-core.l4; this module builds its records from plain answers
-- and restates no rule. Where an answer depends on an earlier question (the kind of applicant, the heads, the
-- maximum), the @desc says which question gives it.
--
-- The Criminal Injuries Compensation Commissioner is an official and gets no seat. The awards are discretionary (s
-- 5(1)): the amount the Commissioner assesses, the Commissioner's satisfactions and opinions (s 5(2), (3A), (4), s
-- 7(1C), (9)) and what the Commissioner chooses to deduct (s 6B) are asked as facts, so each answer is conditional on
-- them.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims of crime assistance (Tasmania) -- the applicant's questions`

-- The criminal conduct, from plain answers.
GIVEN `it was an offence, or would have been but for the offender's age, insanity or another excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involved violence by one person against another`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was a crime under s 127, 127A, 185, 186, 191A or 192 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the offence`                                                   IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Criminal conduct`
`the conduct from my answers` `it was an offence, or would have been but for the offender's age, insanity or another excuse` `it involved violence by one person against another` `it was a crime under s 127, 127A, 185, 186, 191A or 192 of the Criminal Code` `the date of the offence` MEANS
    `Criminal conduct` WITH
        `it is an act of another person that is an offence, or would have been but for the person's age, insanity or other excuse or justification at law` IS `it was an offence, or would have been but for the offender's age, insanity or another excuse`
        `it involves violence by one person against another`                                IS `it involved violence by one person against another`
        `it is a crime under section 127, 127A, 185, 186, 191A or 192 of the Criminal Code` IS `it was a crime under s 127, 127A, 185, 186, 191A or 192 of the Criminal Code`
        `the date of the offence`                                                           IS `the date of the offence`

-- The applicant, from plain answers.
GIVEN `it was committed against me`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was injured in assisting a police officer`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `I suffered an impairment of my bodily or mental health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I became pregnant as a result`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `my injury came from witnessing the offence`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `my relationship to the primary victim`                IS A `Relationship to the primary victim`
      `I paid, or am likely to pay, the funeral expenses`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was dependent on the primary victim`                IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The applicant`
`me from my answers` `it was committed against me` `I was injured in assisting a police officer` `I suffered an impairment of my bodily or mental health` `I became pregnant as a result` `my injury came from witnessing the offence` `my relationship to the primary victim` `I paid, or am likely to pay, the funeral expenses` `I was dependent on the primary victim` MEANS
    `The applicant` WITH
        `the offence was committed against the applicant`                                    IS `it was committed against me`
        `the applicant was injured in assisting a police officer to arrest a person or to prevent the commission of a crime` IS `I was injured in assisting a police officer`
        `the applicant suffered an impairment of bodily or mental health as a result`        IS `I suffered an impairment of my bodily or mental health`
        `the applicant became pregnant as a result`                                          IS `I became pregnant as a result`
        `the applicant's injury resulted from witnessing the offence`                        IS `my injury came from witnessing the offence`
        `the applicant's relationship to the primary victim`                                 IS `my relationship to the primary victim`
        `the applicant incurred, or is reasonably likely to incur, the primary victim's funeral expenses` IS `I paid, or am likely to pay, the funeral expenses`
        `the applicant was dependent on the primary victim`                                  IS `I was dependent on the primary victim`

-- The primary victim, from plain answers.
GIVEN `they were under 18 at the time of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were killed or injured`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `they died as a result`                         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The primary victim`
`the primary victim from my answers` `they were under 18 at the time of the offence` `they were killed or injured` `they died as a result` MEANS
    `The primary victim` WITH
        `was under 18 years of age at the time of the offence` IS `they were under 18 at the time of the offence`
        `was killed or suffered injury as a result`            IS `they were killed or injured` OR `they died as a result`
        `died as a result`                                     IS `they died as a result`

§§ `ss 2 and 4(1)-(1B) -- who can apply`

@export Can I be awarded victims of crime compensation in Tasmania, and as which kind of applicant: primary, secondary or related victim, or the person who paid a primary victim's funeral expenses (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, ss 2, 4)?
GIVEN `it was an offence, or would have been but for the offender's age, insanity or another excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what was done was a criminal offence, or would have been one if the person who did it had not been too young, insane, or excused or justified at law in some other way
      `it involved violence by one person against another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence involved violence by one person against another (the Act covers only such offences, and the crimes in the next question)
      `it was a crime under s 127, 127A, 185, 186, 191A or 192 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a crime under section 127, 127A, 185, 186, 191A or 192 of the Tasmanian Criminal Code (these count even without violence)
      `the date of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The date the offence was committed (funeral expenses can be awarded only for criminal conduct on or after 1 November 2015)
      `it was committed against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was committed against you, so that you are the primary victim
      `I was injured in assisting a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were injured in helping a police officer to arrest someone or to prevent someone committing a crime
      `I suffered an impairment of my bodily or mental health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you suffered any impairment of your physical or mental health as a result (an injury under s 2(2))
      `I became pregnant as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became pregnant as a result of the offence (also an injury under s 2(2))
      `my injury came from witnessing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your injury resulted from witnessing the offence (no if you were not injured)
      `my relationship to the primary victim` IS A `Relationship to the primary victim` @desc Your relationship to the person the offence was committed against, if you are not that person: spouse, child, stepchild, brother, sister, stepbrother, stepsister, parent, step-parent, guardian, in a personal relationship under the Relationships Act 2003, or none of the relationships s 2 names
      `they were under 18 at the time of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the primary victim (the person the offence was committed against) was under 18 at the time of the offence
      `they were killed or injured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the primary victim was killed or injured as a result of the offence
      `they died as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the primary victim died as a result of the offence
      `I paid, or am likely to pay, the funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid, or are reasonably likely to pay, the primary victim's funeral expenses
GIVETH AN `Application answer`
`Can I apply, and as which kind of victim` MEANS
    `the s 4 answer for`
        (`the conduct from my answers` `it was an offence, or would have been but for the offender's age, insanity or another excuse` `it involved violence by one person against another` `it was a crime under s 127, 127A, 185, 186, 191A or 192 of the Criminal Code` `the date of the offence`)
        (`me from my answers` `it was committed against me` `I was injured in assisting a police officer` `I suffered an impairment of my bodily or mental health` `I became pregnant as a result` `my injury came from witnessing the offence` `my relationship to the primary victim` `I paid, or am likely to pay, the funeral expenses` FALSE)
        (`the primary victim from my answers` `they were under 18 at the time of the offence` `they were killed or injured` `they died as a result`)
    -- FALSE: dependence on the primary victim is not read by s 4(1)-(1B) or s 2 (placeholder).

§§ `s 4(1A)-(4) -- what I can claim for`

@export Which heads of compensation can I claim, as the kind of applicant I am (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, s 4(1A)-(4))?
GIVEN `the kind of applicant I apply as` IS A `Kind of applicant` @desc The kind of applicant you apply as: one of the kinds the question "Can I apply, and as which kind of victim" gives you (primary victim; secondary victim by witnessing; secondary victim as parent, step-parent or guardian of a primary victim under 18; related victim; person who incurred a primary victim's funeral expenses)
      `I suffered an impairment of my bodily or mental health` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you yourself suffered any impairment of your physical or mental health as a result of the offence
      `I became pregnant as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became pregnant as a result of the offence
      `my relationship to the primary victim` IS A `Relationship to the primary victim` @desc Your relationship to the primary victim (a parent, step-parent or guardian can claim the expenses of the primary victim's death or injury as a secondary victim)
      `they died as a result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the primary victim died as a result of the offence
      `I was dependent on the primary victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were financially dependent on the primary victim (a related victim of a primary victim who died can claim the financial loss)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Head of compensation`
`Which heads of compensation can I claim` MEANS
    `the heads open to` `the kind of applicant I apply as`
        (`me from my answers` FALSE FALSE `I suffered an impairment of my bodily or mental health` `I became pregnant as a result` FALSE `my relationship to the primary victim` FALSE `I was dependent on the primary victim`)
        (`the primary victim from my answers` FALSE `they died as a result` `they died as a result`)
    -- FALSE placeholders: whether the offence was against me, the police assistance, witnessing, the funeral expenses
    -- and the primary victim's age are not read by s 4(2)-(4) once the kind is known.

§§ `ss 5(2), 5(3A), 5(4), 6 and 12 -- exclusions, and the other schemes`

@export Is my claim excluded, wholly or in part, and which heads are still open (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, ss 5(2), 5(3A), 6, 12)?
GIVEN `the heads I claim` IS A LIST OF `Head of compensation` @desc The heads of compensation you claim, chosen from the answer to "Which heads of compensation can I claim"
      `the heads already paid, or payable, to me under workers compensation` IS A LIST OF `Head of compensation` @desc Any of those heads for which compensation has been paid, or is payable, to you under a law on an employer's compensation for injury or death of its workers (in Tasmania, the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988); empty if none
      `it arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death or injury was caused by, or arose out of, the use of a motor vehicle (within the meaning of the Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999), for example a car driven at someone
      `I also claim for property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you also claim for loss of, or damage to, property
      `I also claim exemplary or aggravated damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you also claim exemplary, vindictive or aggravated damages (damages to punish the offender rather than to make up your loss)
      `I also claim expenses I can claim from Medicare or a health fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of the expenses you claim can be claimed under Medicare or from your registered private health fund
      `the Commissioner is satisfied it resulted from criminal conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied, on the balance of probabilities, that the death or injury resulted from criminal conduct (a conviction is conclusive, s 7(3)); answer yes to see the rest of the answer
      `the Commissioner thinks I failed to help police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the Commissioner's opinion, you failed to do something you reasonably should have done to help identify, apprehend or prosecute the person alleged to have done it
      `it happened before the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the criminal conduct happened before the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976 commenced (on a date fixed by proclamation; it matters only for very old conduct, such as historical child sexual abuse)
GIVETH AN `Exclusion answer`
`Is my claim excluded` MEANS
    `the s 5, s 6 and s 12 answer for` (`Exclusion facts` WITH
        `the Commissioner is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the death or injury was the result of criminal conduct` IS `the Commissioner is satisfied it resulted from criminal conduct`
        `in the Commissioner's opinion the applicant failed to do what they reasonably should have to assist in the identification, apprehension or prosecution of the offender` IS `the Commissioner thinks I failed to help police`
        `the death or injury was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle`  IS `it arose out of the use of a motor vehicle`
        `exemplary, vindictive or aggravated damages are claimed`                        IS `I also claim exemplary or aggravated damages`
        `loss of or damage to property is claimed`                                       IS `I also claim for property`
        `the heads claimed`                                                              IS `the heads I claim`
        `the heads paid, or payable, under a compensation law`                           IS `the heads already paid, or payable, to me under workers compensation`
        `expenses claimable under Medicare or from a registered health benefits organisation are claimed` IS `I also claim expenses I can claim from Medicare or a health fund`
        `the criminal conduct occurred before the Act commenced`                         IS `it happened before the Act commenced`)

@export Does my claim, or part of it, belong to the MAIB motor accidents scheme, workers compensation, or Medicare or a health fund instead (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, s 6(1)(a), (d), (e))?
GIVEN `it arose out of the use of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the death or injury was caused by, or arose out of, the use of a motor vehicle (within the meaning of the Vehicle and Traffic Act 1999)
      `the heads I claim` IS A LIST OF `Head of compensation` @desc The heads of compensation you claim, chosen from the answer to "Which heads of compensation can I claim"
      `the heads already paid, or payable, to me under workers compensation` IS A LIST OF `Head of compensation` @desc Any of those heads paid, or payable, to you under an employer's compensation law (in Tasmania, the Workers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988); empty if none
      `I also claim expenses I can claim from Medicare or a health fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any of the expenses you claim can be claimed under Medicare or from your registered private health fund
GIVETH A LIST OF `Other scheme`
`Does my claim belong to MAIB or workers compensation instead` MEANS
    `the other schemes the exclusions point to` (`Exclusion facts` WITH
        `the Commissioner is satisfied on the balance of probabilities that the death or injury was the result of criminal conduct` IS TRUE
        `in the Commissioner's opinion the applicant failed to do what they reasonably should have to assist in the identification, apprehension or prosecution of the offender` IS FALSE
        `the death or injury was caused by or arose out of the use of a motor vehicle`  IS `it arose out of the use of a motor vehicle`
        `exemplary, vindictive or aggravated damages are claimed`                        IS FALSE
        `loss of or damage to property is claimed`                                       IS FALSE
        `the heads claimed`                                                              IS `the heads I claim`
        `the heads paid, or payable, under a compensation law`                           IS `the heads already paid, or payable, to me under workers compensation`
        `expenses claimable under Medicare or from a registered health benefits organisation are claimed` IS `I also claim expenses I can claim from Medicare or a health fund`
        `the criminal conduct occurred before the Act commenced`                         IS FALSE)
    -- TRUE and FALSE placeholders: s 5(2), s 5(3A), s 6(1)(b)-(c) and s 12 point to no other scheme.

@export Can I be refused because I could sue, and what that I recover from a civil claim must be taken into account (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, s 5(4))?
GIVEN `the Commissioner is satisfied I have, or had, an adequate civil remedy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied you have, or had, an adequate remedy in civil proceedings (for example, suing the offender) for the conduct
      `what I recovered, or would likely recover, by way of damages or compensation` IS A NUMBER @desc The damages or compensation, in dollars, you recovered for the criminal conduct, or that in the Commissioner's opinion you would likely recover if proper action were taken; 0 if none
GIVETH A `Civil remedy answer`
`What does a civil claim do to my award` MEANS
    `the s 5(4) answer for` `the Commissioner is satisfied I have, or had, an adequate civil remedy` `what I recovered, or would likely recover, by way of damages or compensation`

§§ `ss 5(9)-(10), 6A, 6B and reg 4 -- the most I can be awarded, and what is paid`

@export What is the most I can be awarded on this application, in dollars, under the prescribed maxima indexed by the Hobart CPI (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, ss 5(10), 6A; Regulations 2021, reg 4)?
GIVEN `the kind of applicant I apply as` IS A `Kind of applicant` @desc The kind of applicant you apply as, from the answer to "Can I apply, and as which kind of victim" (if you are two kinds, ask once for each)
      `how many offences there were` IS A NUMBER @desc How many offences make up the criminal conduct you apply for: 1 for a single offence; more for a series by the same offender, or by offenders acting together at the same time or one after another (a primary victim of a series has a higher maximum)
      `the date I lodged the application` IS A DATE @desc The date you lodged, or will lodge, the application
      `the date it was or will be decided` IS A DATE @desc The date the Commissioner decided, or is expected to decide, the application (a later date can only give the same or a higher maximum)
      `the Hobart CPI figures` IS A LIST OF NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All Groups) Number for Hobart published by the Australian Bureau of Statistics, each quarter from the March quarter 2020 in order (March, June, September, December), through at least the December quarter before the financial year of the decision
      `what has already been awarded for the same conduct` IS A NUMBER @desc What has already been awarded to you for the same criminal conduct (for example an interim award), in dollars; for funeral expenses, what has been awarded to anyone for the same funeral; 0 if nothing
GIVETH A `Maximum answer`
`What is the most I can be awarded for this application` MEANS
    `the ss 5(10) and 6A answer for` `the kind of applicant I apply as` `how many offences there were` `the date I lodged the application` `the date it was or will be decided` `the Hobart CPI figures` `what has already been awarded for the same conduct`

@export What would be paid to me on an award, after the maximum and any deduction for fines, levies or compensation orders I owe (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, ss 6A, 6B)?
GIVEN `the most I can be awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc The dollar figure from the answer to "What is the most I can be awarded for this application"
      `the amount the Commissioner assesses, apart from future services` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, the Commissioner assesses under the heads you are awarded, other than the cost of future medical, dental, psychological or counselling services (for funeral expenses, the funeral expenses allowed)
      `the amount the Commissioner assesses for future services` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, the Commissioner assesses for medical, dental, psychological or counselling services you will need in the future; 0 if none
      `the Commissioner pays future services on top of the maximum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner determines that the future services amount is paid in addition to the maximum (s 6A(4))
      `what the Commissioner deducts for fines, levies and orders I owe` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount, in dollars, the Commissioner deducts for any fine or other penalty you owe the Crown, any compensation levy you owe under the Victims of Crime Compensation Act 1994, and any unpaid compensation order against you; 0 if none
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`What would be paid to me on an award` MEANS
    `the s 6A and s 6B payment for` `the most I can be awarded` `the amount the Commissioner assesses, apart from future services` `the amount the Commissioner assesses for future services` `the Commissioner pays future services on top of the maximum` `what the Commissioner deducts for fines, levies and orders I owe`

§§ `s 7(1A)-(1D), (8)-(9) -- time limits`

@export By when must I apply for victims of crime compensation (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, s 7(1A)-(1D))?
GIVEN `the date of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The date of the offence your application relates to (for a series of offences the Act does not say which date; give the one you rely on)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (if you were under 18 at the time of the offence and are a primary, secondary or related victim, you have until 3 years after you turn 18)
      `I am a primary, secondary or related victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you apply as a primary, secondary or related victim (no if you only paid for the primary victim's funeral)
      `it involves an allegation of child sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application involves an allegation of child sexual abuse (there is then no time limit)
      `the Commissioner has extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has extended the period to apply because of special circumstances (s 7(1C))
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period as the Commissioner extended it; any date if not extended
GIVETH A `Period to apply`
`By when must I apply` MEANS
    `the s 7 period to apply for` `the date of the offence` `my date of birth` `I am a primary, secondary or related victim` `it involves an allegation of child sexual abuse` `the Commissioner has extended my time` `the extended last day`

@export Is my application in time (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, s 7(1A)-(1D))?
GIVEN `the date of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The date of the offence your application relates to
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `I am a primary, secondary or related victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you apply as a primary, secondary or related victim (no if you only paid for the primary victim's funeral)
      `it involves an allegation of child sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application involves an allegation of child sexual abuse
      `the Commissioner has extended my time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has extended the period to apply because of special circumstances
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period as the Commissioner extended it; any date if not extended
      `the date I lodge the application` IS A DATE @desc The date you lodged, or will lodge, the application with the Victim Assistance Unit
GIVETH AN `In time answer`
`Is my application in time` MEANS
    `the s 7 in-time answer for` (`the s 7 period to apply for` `the date of the offence` `my date of birth` `I am a primary, secondary or related victim` `it involves an allegation of child sexual abuse` `the Commissioner has extended my time` `the extended last day`) `the date I lodge the application`

@export By when is my application to be decided (Victims of Crime Assistance Act 1976, s 7(8)-(9))?
GIVEN `the date I lodged the application` IS A DATE @desc The date of your application
      `the Commissioner has extended the time to decide it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has extended the 3 years for deciding it because of special circumstances (s 7(9))
      `the extended date` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended period; any date if not extended
GIVETH A DATE
`By when is my application to be decided` MEANS
    `the last day to determine an application made on` `the date I lodged the application` `under`
        (IF `the Commissioner has extended the time to decide it`
         THEN `as extended by the Commissioner for special circumstances (s 7(9))` `the extended date`
         ELSE `within 3 years of the date of the application (s 7(8))`)

§§ `reg 5 -- what my application must contain`

@export What must my application for an award contain (Victims of Crime Assistance Regulations 2021, reg 5)?
GIVEN `the kind of applicant I apply as` IS A `Kind of applicant` @desc The kind of applicant you apply as, from the answer to "Can I apply, and as which kind of victim"
      `I apply on behalf of someone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying on behalf of another person (for example a child)
      `I apply because of a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you apply because someone died
      `I was injured assisting a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was suffered in assisting a police officer
GIVETH A LIST OF `Application requirement`
`What must my application contain` MEANS
    `the reg 5 requirements for` `the kind of applicant I apply as` `I apply on behalf of someone else` `I apply because of a death` `I was injured assisting a police officer`
